# Rule: Architecture Compliance Discipline

Before adding or refactoring workflow logic you MUST explicitly snapshot the architecture documents that govern the change:
- `docs/architecture/README.md`
- `docs/architecture/AGENTS_DESIGN.md`
- Relevant workflow doc (e.g., `WHATSAPP_CATALOGING_WORKFLOW.md`)

For each change, document in your explanation how the implementation upholds:
1. Hierarchy & Delegation (Project Manager → Department → Specialist → Tool)
2. Context Engineering (minimal payloads, middleware-based injection)
3. Hexagonal ports/adapters (all external touch points behind interfaces)

If any part of the proposed change deviates from the architecture docs, stop and secure design approval before code.
